<pdd-reason>The single nearest-neighbor tour stranded weak pairs at the end of a set and ignored whether a blend could be snare-matched at all; on the 56-song R&B set, 28 of 55 blends silently fell back to bar-count alignment. Ordering must optimize the whole set and treat backbeat verifiability as part of blend quality.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-interface>
{
  "type": "module",
  "module": {
    "classes": [
      {"name": "MixGraph", "signature": "MixGraph(tracks: list[Track], *, lineage=None, chroma=None, snare_confidence: dict[str, float] | None = None, gate: float = 0.15)", "methods": ["objective(order: list[int]) -> float", "report(order_ids: list[str]) -> list[EdgeReport]"]}
    ],
    "functions": [
      {"name": "optimize_order", "signature": "optimize_order(graph: MixGraph, *, opener_id: str | None = None, time_budget_s: float = 8.0, starts: int = 12) -> list[str]"},
      {"name": "order_summary", "signature": "order_summary(graph: MixGraph, order_ids: list[str]) -> dict"}
    ]
  }
}
</pdd-interface>
<pdd-dependency>brain/mix_graph (pair_score, tempo_step, genre_of, CHROMA_MATCH)</pdd-dependency>

% Goal

Choose the playback order of a finalized set that blends best across the whole set.

% Vocabulary

- **Verifiable blend:** both songs have a snare-parity read at or above the confidence gate, so the builder can match the backbeat (snares on the same counts), not only the beat ticks.
- **Unverified blend:** at least one side's read is below the gate; the builder can only align bar counts.
- **Blind blend:** both sides are below the gate.

% Requirements

1. Edge quality is `mix_graph.pair_score` plus the existing tempo-direction preferences (energy-up bonus, slow-down penalty, no more than two consecutive slow-downs, unbacked genre jumps on cooldown).
2. Unverified blends cost a little and blind blends cost more, so weak-read songs are kept apart and verifiable pairings are preferred when compatibility is otherwise similar.
3. Search the whole order (several deterministic greedy seeds, then 2-opt reversal and 1-3 song moves) within a time budget; never return an order worse than the best seed.
4. `order_summary` reports mean blend score, weak pairs (< 0.5), tempo gaps, and counts of verifiable / unverified / blind blends.

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): the result depends only on the set's contents and analysis; any permutation of the same input returns the identical order (ties break on track_id).
R2 (MUST): every input track appears exactly once.
R3 (MUST): an explicit opener plays first.
R4 (MUST NOT): require a model, network, or audio decode.
</contract_rules>

% Verification

`tests/test_mix_optimizer.py`: shuffled and reversed inputs give the same order; exact-once; not worse than the greedy tour on the objective; opener respected; three weak reads among eight equal songs yield zero blind blends; report labels backbeat status.
